# TextAreaField — label, a multi-line box, hint, error, bound to the caller's
# cell. `TextField` with the one control swapped, and that is the whole diff:
#
#     state note: text = "" @client
#     use TextAreaField("What would you build?", "One or two sentences.", true, "", failed(request), note)
#
# IT COULD NOT BE WRITTEN THIS MORNING, because the language had no `textarea`
# node and this library refuses to fake a control out of another one — a
# single-line `input` styled to look tall still loses everything typed after the
# first Enter, and a field that eats the user's paragraph is worse than no field.
# The node landed with a cell contract checked at the bind site (`a textarea edits
# a text cell`), so `v: cell text` here gets the same three checks a hand-written
# `textarea bind note` gets: that the cell exists, that it is `text`, and that it
# is `@client`.
#
# A SITE WROTE THIS FILE BEFORE THE LIBRARY DID. It needed a "what would you
# build?" box on a request-access form, found no facet, and wrote an exact mirror
# of `TextField` over the same `Field` scaffold — then nominated it for promotion
# on the grounds that a local copy of a library field is a library field in the
# wrong repository. This is that component, unchanged in shape; the site's version
# also had to style `.fa-textarea` itself, and those rules are now in
# `fieldlabel.fct` next to the rules for every other control a `Field` holds.
#
# WHEN TO USE IT INSTEAD OF `TextField`: when the answer is prose. A one-line box
# tells the reader "a few words"; a six-line box tells them "a sentence or two",
# and that expectation is set by the control's height before anything is read. The
# height is `min-height` and `resize: vertical` — the width belongs to the field,
# the height belongs to whoever is writing in it.
import "field.fct"
app FacetForms:
    component TextAreaField(label: text, placeholder: text, required: bool, hint: text, error: text, v: cell text):
        use Field(label, required, hint, error):
            textarea bind v placeholder "{placeholder}"
